WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.116
Keep your muscles.

2
00:00:02.156 --> 00:00:05.997
Here's what weightlessness does to them,
and how the crew fights back.

3
00:00:07.247 --> 00:00:10.640
In weightlessness, your legs and back
barely have to work.

4
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.241
Even holding yourself up takes no effort.

5
00:00:13.281 --> 00:00:16.540
And muscle you don't use, your body stops
maintaining.

6
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.602
Without exercise, you could lose up to
twenty percent

7
00:00:20.602 --> 00:00:22.929
of your muscle mass in about two weeks.

8
00:00:23.829 --> 00:00:26.986
Calves, thighs, and the deep back muscles
go first:

9
00:00:26.986 --> 00:00:29.152
the ones that hold you up on Earth.

10
00:00:30.052 --> 00:00:32.617
That's why the crew trains about two hours
a day.

11
00:00:33.517 --> 00:00:36.863
On the treadmill, a harness pulls you
down, so you can run.

12
00:00:37.763 --> 00:00:42.030
The bike works your heart and lungs. And
the resistance machine builds strength.

13
00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:47.276
Log every session in AURA, so you and
Keiko can follow your progress.

14
00:00:47.316 --> 00:00:51.157
Sharp pain, or a swollen calf? Stop, and
tell Keiko.

15
00:00:52.056 --> 00:00:55.465
Strong legs today mean walking off the
ship on your own.

